---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="TotalRecalls — Own every AI conversation." description="A small Windows app that saves your ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini, and Grok chats into a private folder on your computer — readable Markdown + JSON you keep forever.">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Own every AI conversation.</h1>
    <p class="subhead">A small Windows app that saves your ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini, and Grok chats into a private folder on your computer — readable Markdown + JSON you keep forever.</p>

    <!-- Clean price block: strike-through $49 + $24 launch price -->
    <div class="price-block">
      <span class="price-strike"><strike>$49</strike></span>
      <span class="price-current" data-tr-price>$24</span>
      <span class="price-badge">launch price</span>
      <span class="price-note">One-time purchase · Windows app · Local files only</span>
    </div>

    <p class="cta-group">
      <a href="/buy/" class="buy-button buy-lg" data-tr-buy>Buy TotalRecalls — <span data-tr-price>$24</span></a>
      <a href="/download/" class="buy-button buy-secondary">Already purchased? Download ZIP</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY TOTALRECALLS — 4 pillars with icons -->
  <section class="value-cards">
    <h2>Why TotalRecalls</h2>
    <div class="card icon-permanence"><strong>Your AI history shouldn't vanish.</strong> AI apps change. Tabs close. Exports break. A folder of Markdown on your PC still opens in ten years.</div>
    <div class="card icon-library"><strong>One library for every assistant.</strong> Stop hunting through five different UIs. Export everything into a single, predictable folder structure.</div>
    <div class="card icon-privacy"><strong>Private by design.</strong> Sign-in happens locally. We never host your session tokens. No cloud locker. No account required.</div>
    <div class="card icon-deal"><strong>Simple commercial deal.</strong> One payment. No subscription. No "AI archive" monthly fee.</div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW IT WORKS — 4 steps with icons -->
  <section class="how-it-works">
    <h2>How It Works (4 steps)</h2>
    <ol class="step-list">
      <li><span class="step-icon icon-buy">1</span> <strong>Buy once</strong> — checkout via Lemon Squeezy.</li>
      <li><span class="step-icon icon-install">2</span> <strong>Install</strong> — unzip and run the Windows app.</li>
      <li><span class="step-icon icon-provider">3</span> <strong>Pick a provider</strong> — ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini, or Grok.</li>
      <li><span class="step-icon icon-export">4</span> <strong>Export</strong> — chats land as Markdown + JSON under a Library folder.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- PROVIDERS — logo row -->
  <section class="providers-section">
    <h2>Supported Providers</h2>
    <div class="provider-logos">
      <span>ChatGPT</span>
      <span>Claude</span>
      <span>Perplexity</span>
      <span>Gemini</span>
      <span>Grok</span>
    </div>
    <p class="providers-note">Gemini uses your Google Takeout JSON (most reliable path).</p>
  </section>

  <!-- SCREENSHOTS / PROOF -->
  <section class="screenshots">
    <h2>Your Library, organized</h2>
    <div class="screenshot-grid">
      <div class="screenshot-card">
        <div class="app-mock" role="img" aria-label="Library folder structure">
          <div class="app-mock-titlebar">
            <span class="dot red"></span><span class="dot yellow"></span><span class="dot green"></span>
            <span class="app-mock-title">TotalRecalls — Library</span>
          </div>
          <div class="app-mock-body">
            <div class="app-mock-sidebar">
              <strong>Library</strong>
              <span>ChatGPT</span>
              <span>Claude</span>
              <span>Perplexity</span>
              <span>Gemini</span>
              <span>Grok</span>
            </div>
            <div class="app-mock-files">
              <div class="file-row"><code>chatgpt/2026-08-01-pricing-research.md</code><span>12 KB</span></div>
              <div class="file-row"><code>claude/2026-07-28-refactor-plan.md</code><span>31 KB</span></div>
              <div class="file-row"><code>perplexity/2026-07-21-market-scan.md</code><span>8 KB</span></div>
              <div class="file-row"><code>gemini/2026-07-14-takeout-thread.md</code><span>19 KB</span></div>
              <div class="file-row"><code>grok/2026-07-02-debug-session.md</code><span>6 KB</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>Every assistant exports into a clean folder structure you can browse, search, and back up.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="screenshot-card">
        <div class="app-mock" role="img" aria-label="Readable Markdown chat file">
          <div class="app-mock-titlebar">
            <span class="dot red"></span><span class="dot yellow"></span><span class="dot green"></span>
            <span class="app-mock-title">2026-08-01-pricing-research.md</span>
          </div>
          <div class="app-mock-md">
            <div class="md-h"># Pricing research</div>
            <div class="md-meta">exported 2026-08-01 · provider: chatgpt · 14 messages</div>
            <div class="md-you"><strong>You:</strong> Compare one-time pricing for export tools.</div>
            <div class="md-ai"><strong>Assistant:</strong> Here is a table of the options I found, with links and caveats…</div>
            <div class="md-meta">+ attachments: sources.json</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>Readable files. Predictable formatting. Easy to diff, annotate, or feed into your own tools.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- GUIDES -->
  <section class="guides-teaser">
    <h2>Guides (SEO + how-to)</h2>
    <p class="guides-intro">Free reading. Buy only when you want the Windows app.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/guides/export-chatgpt-conversations/">How to export ChatGPT conversations</a> — Official export vs a local library you can actually use</li>
      <li><a href="/guides/export-claude-chat-history/">Download your Claude chat history</a> — Keep Projects and long threads as files</li>
      <li><a href="/guides/backup-perplexity-threads/">Backup Perplexity threads</a> — Save research threads before you lose the tab trail</li>
      <li><a href="/guides/gemini-takeout-archive/">Gemini Takeout → readable archive</a> — Turn Google Takeout dumps into Markdown conversations</li>
      <li><a href="/guides/own-your-ai-chat-data/">Own your AI chat data</a> — Why multi-assistant export matters in 2026</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- TECHNICAL NOTES (replaces Straight Talk — softer framing) -->
  <section class="technical-notes">
    <h2>Technical Notes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Windows app today (WebView2). Mac later if demand is real.</li>
      <li>Gemini uses your Google Takeout folder/JSON (most reliable path).</li>
      <li>Unsigned builds may show SmartScreen — “More info → Run anyway” until code-signing is complete.</li>
      <li>SP8 Smart App Control can block unsigned apps with no override — signing is on the roadmap.</li>
      <li>You must follow each AI provider's terms for your own account use.</li>
      <li>No AdSense clutter. This site sells a tool, not pageviews.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="faq-section">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <dl>
      <dt>Can I use this on Mac?</dt>
      <dd>V2 is Windows-only. Mac is planned if demand is real.</dd>
      <dt>Will my provider block me?</dt>
      <dd>TotalRecalls works within each provider's own export/Takeout features — you must follow their terms.</dd>
      <dt>Is there a refund policy?</dt>
      <dd>All sales are final (digital download). Try the free guides first.</dd>
      <dt>How do I get updates?</dt>
      <dd>Minor updates are free during the launch period and posted to this site.</dd>
    </dl>
    <p class="faq-more"><a href="/faq/">More questions</a></p>
  </section>

  <!-- FOOTER CTA — single clean CTA -->
  <section class="footer-cta">
    <h2>Ready to own your AI conversations?</h2>
    <div class="footer-price">
      <span class="price-strike"><strike>$49</strike></span>
      <span class="price-current" data-tr-price>$24</span>
      <span class="price-badge">launch price</span>
    </div>
    <a href="/buy/" class="buy-button buy-lg" data-tr-buy>Buy TotalRecalls — <span data-tr-price>$24</span></a>
    <p><a href="/download/">Already purchased? Download ZIP</a></p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
